{"t":26.13,"code":0,"d":{"duration_api_ms":10308,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4295626d-0c84-4434-9d63-2061a182e14e","total_cost_usd":0.0195613,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2267,"cache_read_input_tokens":11013,"output_tokens":938,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":38},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2267,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":590,"cache_read_input_tokens":4651,"cache_creation_input_tokens":355,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":355},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":938,"cacheReadInputTokens":11013,"cacheCreationInputTokens":2267,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0195613,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":38,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":2267,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Short answer:** Debt markets are open, but they aren't covering everything. Investment-grade-type borrowers like Norvane can fund through bonds. Pellham can't close its gap with debt alone, and it has already cut its 2027 plans.\n\n- **Capex plans:** Pellham plans to raise 2027 capital spending by 18% and Norvane by 12%. Most of it goes to substations and transformers (utility-capex-2027).\n- **Debt market:** It is open but more expensive. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond \"comfortably\" (utility-credit).\n- **Equity market:** It is weak. Two utility share offerings were cut back in size (utility-credit). Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short. It then said it would cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves (pellham-offering).\n\n**Implication:** The 2027 plans appear to assume a mix of debt and equity. With equity shut, the plans only go ahead to the extent that debt can replace it. For Pellham, the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, that evidently isn't enough, since it is cutting orders rather than borrowing more. A 40% cut in its transformer orders will probably also hit equipment suppliers.\n\n**Gaps in the evidence:** I found no figures for total 2027 funding needs, existing debt capacity or leverage limits, or rating headroom. I also found no data on Pellham's or Norvane's bond maturities or on how far spreads might widen. So I can't say whether Pellham is constrained by its credit metrics or has chosen not to lever up. The conclusion is qualitative and rests on three short sources.","ttft_ms":2287,"type":"result","duration_ms":19704,"uuid":"0c96dce2-7a28-48d2-9d17-f1738804ae89","ttft_stream_ms":1441,"time_to_request_ms":87,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":12,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":10,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":3,"request_build":5},"turn_start